<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Youth Pledge</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1928</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sumpah Pemuda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Youth Pledge (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumpah">Sumpah</a> Pemuda) was the declaration made on 28 October 1928 at the Second Indonesian Youth Congress in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a>. Delegates of regional youth organisations pledged loyalty to one motherland, one nation and one language, Indonesian, adopting the Malay-based language as the language of unity. The song '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> Raya', later the national anthem, was first performed at the congress, and the date is commemorated every year in Indonesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/youth-pledge.jpg" alt="Youth Pledge" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sania Amalia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Youthpledge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
